From 51f0dd7d1d85a1a060301c0f3d0bc1221184160a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:24:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: add C-PHY support and switch surya's
 IMX682 to it

THE CAMERA WORKS. After months of investigation, the sensor delivers frames.

Root cause: the IMX682 on this board is a C-PHY transmitter and the receiver
was configured for D-PHY. Its CSI_SIGNALING_MODE register (0x0111) is set to
0x03 by both the vendor blob and our driver, which the MIPI CCS specification
defines as CSI-2 C-PHY, and it reads back as such from the live hardware. The
three 'lanes' are three trios; there is no separate clock lane.

That explains every symptom the investigation ever recorded: not a single SOT
captured, zero CRC and zero ECC errors, electrical activity on the pins but no
link, error bits on some lanes and none on 'lane 0', the CSID TPG working (it
bypasses the PHY), the settle count sweep achieving nothing across the whole
MIPI window (T_HS_SETTLE is a D-PHY parameter), and every register comparison
against the factory coming out identical: the sensor configuration was copied
faithfully, C-PHY mode included, and the receiver was never questioned.

  camss.c        accept V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_CPHY and remember which one it is
  camss-csiphy.h carry the bus type in the CSI-2 config
  camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
                 csiphy_sm7150_config_trios(): C-PHY has no clock lane, the
                 trios enable the ODD bits of CTRL5, the tuning registers are a
                 different set (transcribed from the vendor's csiphy_3ph_v1_2_reg,
                 three trios by 38 settings) and the settle count is two bytes
  camss-csid.h / camss-csid.c
                 propagate the bus type to the receiver
  camss-csid-gen2.c
                 set CSI2_RX_CFG0 bit 24 (PHY_TYPE_SEL) for C-PHY; mainline
                 never wrote it, so it always decoded as D-PHY
  imx682.c       parse the endpoint as C-PHY instead of hardcoding D-PHY
  sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
                 bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_CPHY> on both endpoints and
                 drop clock-lanes, which only exists in D-PHY

Verified on a POCO X3 NFC: 5 frames of 20109824 bytes each, 199829 non-zero
bytes per 200000, min 0 max 255 mean 56.2 stddev 50.8 over 256 distinct values.
Real image data, not a stuck pattern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
